# =============================================================================
# Common Pose — .gitignore
#
# Policy: this repository redistributes NO third-party data, NO checkpoints and NO
# large experiment outputs. What it DOES track is source code plus the small frozen
# evidence artifacts under `audits/`, `experiments/*/results/` and `docs/` that are
# the published result.
#
# Directories below are anchored with a leading `/` wherever they describe a
# project-root location. An unanchored pattern such as `artifacts/` or `logs/` matches
# at ANY depth, which silently excludes the frozen audit artifacts this repository
# exists to publish. That exact defect was caught by comparing `git ls-files` against
# the working tree, and is why the anchoring here is explicit.
# =============================================================================

# --- datasets and raw data (never redistributed) -----------------------------
/data/
/datasets/
/raw_data/
/external/
/downloads/
/scratch/
raw/
data/
datasets/

# --- model weights and checkpoints -------------------------------------------
/checkpoints/
/models/
*.ckpt
*.pth
*.pt
*.safetensors
*.onnx
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.mat
*.npz
*.npy
*.pkl
*.pickle
*.joblib
*.bin
*.parquet
*.feather
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.7z

# --- experiment outputs and caches, root-anchored -----------------------------
/outputs/
/runs/
/wandb/
/mlruns/

# Bare names that mean "generated scratch" wherever they appear.
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.py[cod]
*.so
*.dylib
*.dll
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Logs and figures are generated, EXCEPT the captured stdout that the audit lanes
# publish as evidence. Those live under `audits/` and are re-included below.
*.log
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.mp4
*.pdf

# --- build products ----------------------------------------------------------
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.tox/
.coverage
htmlcov/
coverage.xml
*.prof

# --- environments ------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
.venv-*/
venv/
env/
ENV/
conda/
.env
.env.*
*.env

# --- editors and OS ----------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- secrets and machine-local configuration --------------------------------
*.pem
*.key
*.ppk
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
.ssh/
credentials*
*secret*
*token*
!*token*.md

# --- project-specific scratch conventions ------------------------------------
# The historical research workspace used these prefixes for reconnaissance and
# one-shot patch scripts. They are excluded from the evidence chain by the audit
# plans and must not enter the public repository.
_patch*.py
_recon_*.py
_audit_s*/
_verify_s*/
_tmp*/
*.tmp

# =============================================================================
# Re-include the frozen evidence. Everything here is small, hand-curated, and is
# the actual published result. Listed AFTER the exclusions so it wins.
# =============================================================================
!audits/**/*.json
!audits/**/*.csv
!audits/**/*.md
!audits/**/*.txt
!audits/**/*.log
!experiments/**/results/*.json
!experiments/**/*.md
!provenance/**/*.json
!provenance/**/*.sha256
!docs/**/*.json
!docs/**/*.csv
!docs/**/*.md
!docs/**/*.txt
!src/**/*.md
!scripts/**/*.py
!tests/**/*.py
!*.md
!*.txt
